# Mini-Lesson 24.6: Introduction to Node.js

---

# Overview

This lesson introduces Node.js, an open-source JavaScript runtime environment used to execute JavaScript code outside of a web browser.

In Module 10, Node.js was used to make API calls. In Module 24, Node.js will be used to:

- Create web applications
- Build a web server
- Consume Kafka messages
- Display streaming data
- Support Required Project 24.2

Node.js becomes the consumer layer that receives Kafka messages and serves them through a web application.

---

# What is Node.js?

Node.js is:

- Open-source
- Cross-platform
- Server-side JavaScript runtime
- Event-driven
- Lightweight
- High-performance

Supported platforms include:

- Windows
- Linux
- Unix
- macOS

